			"notes": "## What's Changed in v2.1.0\n\n\n* **1:1 Spigot Permissions Support**: Fully integrated with Fabric's permission API (`fabric-permissions-api-v1`), compatible with LuckPerms and vanilla OP levels.\n  * Supported nodes: `imageframe.create`, `imageframe.get`, `imageframe.get.others`, `imageframe.delete`, `imageframe.delete.others`, `imageframe.rename`, `imageframe.rename.others`, `imageframe.refresh`, `imageframe.refresh.others`, `imageframe.playback`, `imageframe.select`, `imageframe.list`, `imageframe.list.others`, `imageframe.info`, `imageframe.reload`, and `imageframe.admin`.\n* **Map Ownership & Anti-Grief**: Non-OP players can only manage and retrieve their own created maps. Managing other players' maps strictly requires `.others` permissions or `imageframe.admin`.\n* **Empty Maps Requirement (`RequireEmptyMaps`)**: When enabled, survival players must have enough empty maps in their inventory to create or get maps.\n* **Streamlined & Functional `config.yml`**:\n  * Removed legacy Spigot relics (fake web server on port 8517, MySQL/JDBC, ViaVersion hooks, SpigotMC updater, and Bukkit threading hacks).\n  * 100% of remaining options are actively enforced by the Fabric mod (`Language`, `DateFormat`, `RequireEmptyMaps`, `CombinedByDefault`, `MaxSize`, `RestrictImageUrl`, `MaxImageFileSize`, `MaxProcessingTime`, `PlayerCreationLimit`, `InvisibleFrame`).\n* **Config Auto-Healing**:\n  * Solved flat classloader collision that previously caused Floodgate's config to be copied into `config/ImageFrame/config.yml`.\n  * Automatically detects 0-byte or Floodgate configs on startup, backs them up to `config.yml.bak`, and generates the authentic ImageFrame configuration without manual intervention.\n* **Live Reload**: `/imageframe reload` reloads both `config.yml` and localized language files without server restart."
		},
